**Drift-aware change sets have a known limitation:**

```
Drift-aware change sets require CloudFormation to first
run a drift detection scan on all 22 existing resources
before it can build the change set.

If ANY resource in the stack has drifted from the
template — meaning someone changed it manually in
the console — the drift-aware mode can fail with
"Internal Failure" during the pre-scan phase.

It does NOT mean your template has errors.
```

---

**What likely happened:**

```
Your live stack has resources that were updated
outside of CloudFormation — for example:

- The IAM role was modified directly
- The Lambda function code was updated via console
- The S3 bucket policy was edited manually
- The Cognito client was changed in console

CloudFormation saw drift, got confused during the
drift-aware pre-validation, and threw Internal Failure
instead of a useful error message.

This is a known AWS bug with drift-aware change sets
on stacks that have inline Lambda ZipFile code.
```

